<!--
  Every <loc> here is a CANONICAL, 200-returning URL — verified live 2026-09-16.

  What was wrong before, and why it is easy to get wrong again: this file listed
  eight URLs, six of which were not canonical.
    · /features.html /plans.html /compare.html /download.html  → 301 to the
      extensionless form. A sitemap must list the destination, not the redirect.
    · /landing          → 404 on veyrnox.com. That is a route of THIS app
      (LandingGuard, src/App.jsx), which is served from veyrnox-prod.pages.dev,
      not from the veyrnox.com apex.
    · /veyrnox-docs.html → 301 to /veyrnox-docs, which is 404 on veyrnox.com.
      That file exists in this repo's public/ and is served from the Pages host.
  With the `/* /index.html 200` SPA fallback in _redirects, a bad path does not
  404 — it returns 200 and the app shell, i.e. a SOFT 404. That is why six dead
  entries survived here unnoticed: nothing ever returned an error code.

  KNOWN, DELIBERATELY NOT CHANGED HERE: this file is served from
  veyrnox-prod.pages.dev but declares veyrnox.com URLs, and veyrnox.com serves
  its own /sitemap-index.xml (our /sitemap.xml 301s to it there). Deciding which
  host should be indexed is a site-ownership call, not a correctness fix, so this
  pass only makes every listed URL resolve. Do not "tidy" the host without an
  owner decision — veyrnox.com is a separate codebase (see CLAUDE.md).
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://veyrnox.com/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
